  "Question": "Let \\(y=mx+b\\) be the image when the line \\(x-3y+11=0\\) is reflected across the \\(x\\)-axis. The value of \\(m+b\\) is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-6\\)",
    "B": "\\(-5\\)",
    "C": "\\(-4\\)",
    "D": "\\(-3\\)",
    "E": "\\(-2\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Reflection across the \\(x\\)-axis keeps each point's \\(x\\)-coordinate and negates its \\(y\\)-coordinate. First write the original line as\n\\[y=\\frac{x+11}{3}.\\]\nNegating its output gives the reflected line\n\\[y=-\\frac{x+11}{3}=-\\frac13x-\\frac{11}{3}.\\]\nThus \\(m=-1/3\\) and \\(b=-11/3\\), so\n\\[m+b=-\\frac{12}{3}=\\boxed{-4}.\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
